{"body":{"text":["*Awaiting the author's ratification. Unlike the rest of Knowledge, which is to be rewritten whole once the elevation is done (23/152), Keeping the field and its Elevation are written as the work is now to be done, and are marked ratified once he has read and accepted them (23/152).*"]},"id":"1M89M0X5Y7E4000","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["What a session knows is in the field; memory is off, \"OpenLight had to set this boundary early\" (2/6). A session is kept whole in his words, every utterance as said, its answers by their essence, read against the transcripts by blank readers until nothing is distorted and nothing important lost (13/129, 23/138). What matters in it is lifted into the elevation, below."]},"id":"1M89M0X5Y7E4001","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["Then Knowledge is written: what is to be conveyed considered first, the briefs worked with in the large and the small, then checked under the rule, against the session, and as a whole for distortions and conflicts, round upon round until no scrutiny comes back; then the author reads it, and once he approves, the next session may start (23/138). Knowledge is written whole, never patched: \"patching, I think, is forbidden under the rules\" (23/144)."]},"id":"1M89M0X5Y7E4002","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["Reading every session to be aligned is \"probably going to be a debt soon\"; \"we haven't purified the knowledge\" (15/1, 15/3). Knowledge is that purifying, regenerated whole when the sessions have moved past it, as it is to be once the elevation is done (23/152)."]},"id":"1M89M0X5Y7E4003","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["How far the code has come changes quickly, and the author doubted keeping it here: \"That makes it very short-lived because it now has to stay true to everything. I'm not sure we want that. But maybe it's valuable.\" (15/7). *Proposed:* each part says it in a line, said again when the part is regenerated."]},"id":"1M89M0X5Y7E4004","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["The field is written today by the author's tools in `author/`, through the engine: `session.ts` keeps a session, `append.ts` adds an utterance, and `rewrite.ts` writes briefs. What they still do for threads, paths, cycles and measures, `thread.ts` among them, is no part of the work. The tools are to go, the author's direction being away from rigid scripts toward clear types and structure and practices held as skills, so an agent knows how to work and does the work with the engine directly (15/31); the command line able to commit was to replace them (settled 2026-11-11). Whether they go before that or wait for commits written in the field he left open, and for now they stay, with this note: \"I don't know if we should remove them yet, or if we're waiting for the better commit expressions to come in place\" (23/146, 23/148). *Open.*"]},"id":"1M89M0X5Y7E4005","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["`rewrite.ts` can change words inside a paragraph it keeps, which invites the patching the author holds forbidden (23/144); the twenty-third session patched so (23/145). A brief keeps its id when written anew; its paragraphs and sentences are given new holons."]},"id":"1M89M0X5Y7E4006","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["A question is held in the field as a statement whose status is open: \"if something is a question, make it. In the substrate.\" (10/8, 23/79)."]},"id":"1M89M0X5Y7E4007","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["What a session did is committed before it ends, and no session starts on another's uncommitted work: \"We never want to start off a session with local changes.\" (4/2)."]},"id":"1M89M0X5Y7E4008","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["The elevation is what was said, lifted so the author can look upon all of it at once and see only what is important (23/50, 23/52): \"I want to be able to plot up all of the steps, put things into perspective, and from there, naturally being able to prioritize and not\" (23/50). Threads alone could not give that: \"just threads to me is a little bit of chaos, probably\" (23/50). Less is more, and whatever is newly lifted looks first upon what is already there (23/62)."]},"id":"1M89M0X5Y7E4009","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["*The elevation as drawn here is the author's leaning, 23/50 to 23/138, at his \"everything looks fine\" (23/132); what the session added is marked as the session's where it stands.*"]},"id":"1M89M0X5Y7E400A","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["There are three levels. The ground is the sessions and their utterances, as they are kept. Knowledge stands on top, briefs written under the rule. Between them stands the elevation: \"the bottom level being the source, the discussions, the top level being the briefs, and this being the intermediate layer\" (23/94). The elevation tells what was said and where; Knowledge tells what holds and why (23/90, 23/91)."]},"id":"1M89M0X5Y7E400B","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["A **statement** is one sentence written under the rule, saying first what it conveys: \"statements and everything should honor the nature of what they are, and if they are something to do, if they are a task, if they are an action, they should be named appropriately\" (23/98). So a task is named as the doing, and what was objected to is written as what is held instead, as the session drew it (23/119). Whether one sentence is enough the author asks, though \"I appreciate the idea that it should be\" (23/116); the session allowed a second, for its reason only (23/129)."]},"id":"1M89M0X5Y7E400C","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["A statement has no name and no address of its own; it is reached by its id (23/115, 23/116). It points at its ground, the utterances or sentences it rests on, the author's words or the session's (23/80), which components might show by their numbers (23/116)."]},"id":"1M89M0X5Y7E400D","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["Every statement has a **status**, where it stands now: open, asked and not decided; proposed, the session's and not taken up; leaning, the author's, inclined to with doubt; settled, decided by the author; closed, no longer holding. These are Knowledge's own marks, with closed beside them. Each status points at what gave it, the utterance of the decision, and so whose it was, as the session drew it (23/129). A statement's history is its versions (23/132)."]},"id":"1M89M0X5Y7E400E","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["Closed points at what closed it, a statement, a commit, a brief or the author's word (23/135), and may be opened again: \"Knowledge is built on its grounds, and any new ground may always exist, shifting the landscape of other pieces of knowledge\" (23/138). The reader holding all the sessions offered set aside or closed (23/137), and the author chose closed: \"Closed is probably better. It's more precise\", where set aside \"tells more about the reason and might be wrong in that\" (23/138)."]},"id":"1M89M0X5Y7E400F","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["A statement that is something to do also has **work**: to do, or done, pointing at the commit that did it. Settled is not done, since a decided fact or principle has nothing left to do (23/124, 23/125). When the work is done the statement is said again as what now holds: \"The work point about the statement being written to what now holds makes sense\" (23/132). What is planned to be built is every statement whose work is still to do."]},"id":"1M89M0X5Y7E400G","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["A **topic** is a type of its own, a short name holding statements: \"topics need short names because topics naturally are addressable\" (23/116). A statement may stand in several topics, the session's answer (23/111). Topics may hold topics, \"you can structure a group and there's a hierarchy in and of itself\" (23/86), though whether the reader's six groups are such he did not know (23/110); of topics and statements composing he said, \"Yeah, why not?\" (23/112)."]},"id":"1M89M0X5Y7E400H","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["A topic's spans are where it was spoken of, each written between(session, from, to) (23/79, 23/80). They are read from its statements' grounds, as the session drew it (23/129), and written by hand only where the topic reaches beyond them: \"It itself may extend its spans above the statement\" (23/110). A topic with nothing in Knowledge yet is, as the session put it, a debt in plain sight (23/91)."]},"id":"1M89M0X5Y7E400J","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["Work that belongs together is gathered in a brief in Knowledge, and its order is written there as prose: \"We don't need to have structured and typed data for project management\" (23/100); the groups \"can be made by briefs\" (23/116). How a brief's flow is to hold statements, beside paragraphs, lists, code and briefs, is a question the twenty-third session raised. *Open, the session's.*"]},"id":"1M89M0X5Y7E400K","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["Threads, paths and cycles go once the sessions are drawn anew: \"Yes, threads and paths are let go, but so is more things, cycles, etc.\" (23/110). Condensations and measures go with them on the session's list, which he did not contest (23/111, 23/112), though he once thought measures might be a dimension of their own (23/52). Until the redraw, what goes stays in the field as it is, and is no part of the work."]},"id":"1M89M0X5Y7E400M","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["Statistics and their board may stay for now, still an idea worth pursuing, though the system was never ready for them (23/52)."]},"id":"1M89M0X5Y7E400N","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["Glass's values, sovereignty and one source of truth among them, \"ought to be a brief somewhere anyway, probably\" (23/62)."]},"id":"1M89M0X5Y7E400P","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["A reader drew every session in an earlier form of this, as 48 topics and 459 statements, with a page made to look upon them (23/85 to 23/89); a final pass found 420 of the 459 fitting, and the model was changed by what it found (23/129, 23/137)."]},"id":"1M89M0X5Y7E400Q","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["The elevation gives what, not why: the reasoning, the turns of a talk and the author's state stay in the sessions and in Knowledge (23/93)."]},"id":"1M89M0X5Y7E400R","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["Knowledge is to hold this practice whole, as a skill, so the next session can do it from Knowledge alone: \"the knowledge holon should contain naturally everything because it's a skill\" (23/130, 23/131). Its steps: the types, statement and topic, written with their moulds; the twelfth, eighteenth and twenty-third sessions drawn and read back by a blank reader; then every session drawn and the work gathered in briefs; then threads, paths, cycles, condensations and measures let go, and Knowledge rewritten whole (23/129, 23/131, 23/152)."]},"id":"1M89M0X5Y7E400S","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
